# BTL path parity for the Render candidate.
#
# Render serves this file the same way the other sites in this repo use theirs
# (ri, toss, fplb, px, cgg). Everything here exists so a path that worked on the
# SiteGround property does not become a 404 the day DNS moves.

# Retired with the SiteGround property. The content is not in this repo, so
# this is a holding redirect, not a replacement: if it is exported it gets its
# own folder here and this line comes out.
#
# This is not a small wildcard. Search Console reports 35 distinct URLs under
# this prefix drawing impressions, including a full Spanish (/es/) set. Sending
# all of them to the homepage is a deliberate, lossy holding measure — Google
# reads a mass redirect to an unrelated page as a soft 404 and will drop them.
# It beats 35 hard 404s and nothing else here beats it until the content exists.
/phillips-law/*  /  301

# The tort shortcuts predate the /campaigns/ layout. They are still referenced
# by 404.html and by anything linking to the old estate, so keep the old shapes
# resolving instead of sending people from one 404 into another. /dupixent/ is
# not hypothetical: it is this property's best-performing URL (55 impressions,
# 3 clicks, average position 8.4 over the six months to 2026-09-22).
/talc/*          /campaigns/talc/          301
/hair-relaxer/*  /campaigns/hair-relaxer/  301
/dupixent/*      /campaigns/dupixent/      301
/depo-provera/*  /campaigns/depo-provera/  301
/glp-1/*         /campaigns/glp-1/         301
/sex-abuse/*     /campaigns/sexual-abuse/  301
